A||||17||88FORMULA-T-TOP-GUY||Whats the dif between an Formula and a Coupe?||||1||
Z||000000||88FORMULA-T-TOP-GUY||05-02-2001||01:26 PM||||I have what I beleive to be a Formula. It says it on the side anyway. Could it be a Coupe with Formula lettering?  I saw a picture of a Coupe and it looked the same. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||05-02-2001||01:33 PM||||Except for the "FORMULA" on the doors, they look the same from the outside. Also, I think the formula was stock with a rear wing. Formula's were only made in 88. They had a V6 unlike the coupe's L4.<P>You checked your VIN# yet?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000002||gt2437||05-02-2001||01:34 PM||||Formula's are '88 GT's in a coupe body  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-02-2001||01:37 PM||||did you happen to get this formula from a guy south of LA on an ebay auction that ended this last Sunday night?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-02-2001||01:37 PM||||BTW the Formula also has the factory rear sway bar, which the coupe lacks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Galen||05-02-2001||01:39 PM||||a Formula is not a GT with a coupe body.. its a coupe with a v6, wing, and lace wheels.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">`<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-02-2001||01:39 PM||||BTW the Formula also has the factory rear sway bar, which the coupe lacks, and I believe the suspension all around is stiffer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||05-02-2001||01:40 PM||||Check the VIN number against the chart here:<P> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/VIN-number.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/VIN-number.html</A> <P><BR>Should be an 88 coupe body style with a V6 engine if it's an original Formula...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero5||05-02-2001||01:40 PM||||Formulas also have the WS6 suspension package, where the coupe only has the W66 suspension.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                                                                                                                          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3_new_Fiero_beauty's-side2.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000009||Formula||05-02-2001||01:47 PM||||formula's also have very low options, usually only options are air cond, power brakes, cassette, and other small ones.... rarely do you find one with pw, equalizer, subwoofer, leather etc...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||88FORMULA-T-TOP-GUY||05-02-2001||01:49 PM||||So what is the difference between the WS6 and W66 suspensions?  By the way, mine looks identical the black Formula pictured above except is a T top. The lettering is grey on the outside and purple on the inside. Was that original????||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula||05-02-2001||01:49 PM||||also, the formula is a gt with a coupe body.  the suspension is the gt type.  if it was a coupe with a v6 then it wouldnt handle as well..  but it would be lighter and faster so that might have been a good trade off!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula||05-02-2001||01:53 PM||||the ws6 has stiffer struts and shocks, a rear sway bar, bigger tires, the front sits higher then the back (ugly but functional).<P>the w66 is just a normal passenger car suspension..<BR>------------------------<BR>the pre 88 suspensions are easier to modify and a lot cheaper to work on...<P>the 88 suspensions are hard to find parts for, more expensive, but they are a little nicer on your bum<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||ray b||05-02-2001||03:10 PM||||I got one of each 88 formula and fake [v-6 swap]<BR>other than sway bar in rear formulas have 120 speedos and extra gages and stronger rear springs [codes=c in coupes ,D in formulas]  auto tran gear diffrent. vin is best way to tell if it is real.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||05-02-2001||03:28 PM||||In the VIN number the 5th digit is an E for the coupe and the Formula, and the 8th digit is a 9 for the Forumula only.<P> Only the Forumula came with the V6 (9 @ the 8th digit) - the coupes were all 2.5L.<P>here is a decoder page you can read all the details on:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.nytmare.org/fiero/vin/fierovin.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nytmare.org/fiero/vin/fierovin.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Black88GT||05-02-2001||09:02 PM||||Power brakes was an option???<P>You can fix the " '88 squat" (as I like to call it) very easily, buy KYB struts.  It raises it just enough to be even with the front.  Works well I have found...<P>||||reg||14
Z||000016||KissMySSFiero||05-02-2001||09:37 PM||||in all pontiacs..including firebirds.   any car that is labeled formula is a cheaper gt/trans am model.  they made it to let you have better performance at lower cost.  therefore you wont have the options and look like the gt or TA.  pontiac didnt offer formulas with the other options because it would cost as much as a gt if they did that.  i think the options you couldnt get were the performance sound, leather, power mirrors, lumbar seats, leather steering wheel, and the formula came with lesser performance tires(i think) than the gt.  i believe gt's had h rated tires.  however the formula did come stock with a spoiler, 120speedo, aux guages, gt rims(black only) v6, and im sure theres  more but this is all i can think of now.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000017||88FORMULA-T-TOP-GUY||05-03-2001||04:56 AM||||Thanks to everyone for all of the great info.<BR>I ran my vin# and found that I definitely have an original T-top Formula. I bought it a year ago in great shape other than drivers seat, clutch and cracked exhaust manifold with 88k miles for $1,400.00.  Great cars.||||reg||1
